524	     * Skips over and discards <code>n</code> bytes of data from the
525	     * input stream.
526	     *
527	     *The <code>skip</code> method skips over some smaller number of bytes
528	     * when reaching end of file before <code>n</code> bytes have been skipped.
529	     * The actual number of bytes skipped is returned.  If <code>n</code> is
530	     * negative, no bytes are skipped.
531	     *
532	     * @param      n   the number of bytes to be skipped.
533	     * @return     the actual number of bytes skipped.
534	     * @exception  IOException  if an I/O error occurs.
535	     *             ChecksumException if the chunk to skip to is corrupted
536	     */
537	    @Override
